9. Common Mistakes
Mistake 1
onClick={hello()}

❌ Wrong

Runs immediately.

Correct

onClick={hello}


Mistake 2

Using lowercase

onclick

Wrong.

React uses camelCase.

Correct

onClick


Mistake 3

Forgetting arrow function when passing arguments.

Wrong

onClick={deleteUser(2)}

Correct

onClick={() => deleteUser(2)}

🐞 Debugging Techniques
Use console.log() inside event handlers:
function handleClick() {
  console.log("Button clicked");
}
Inspect the event object:
function handleChange(event) {
  console.log(event);
}
Check the browser's developer console for errors.
Verify that you passed a function reference, not a function call.

⚡ Performance Tips
Don't create unnecessarily complex inline arrow functions inside very large lists.
Keep event handler functions focused on one task.
Name handlers clearly:
handleClick
handleSubmit
handleChange
For most apps, simple inline arrow functions are perfectly fine. Optimize only when profiling shows a real performance issue.

💼 Industry Best Practices

Prefix handler names with handle:

function handleSubmit() {}
function handleLogin() {}
Keep business logic separate from JSX when possible.
Validate user input inside event handlers before updating state.



